**Fix complete.** 

The bug was in `advanceTurn` at line 43 of `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmpfcpfseqj/run/src/sim.ts`. The condition was:

```typescript
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {  // BUG: allows growth when surplus is exactly 0
  population += 1;
}
```

I changed it to:

```typescript
if (foodSurplus > 0) {  // FIXED: only grow when there's an actual surplus
  population += 1;
}
```

**Why this fixes the bug:**
- The comment says "population grows by 1 if there was a food surplus this turn"
- "Surplus" means a **positive** amount, not zero
- Previously, the code allowed population growth when food production equaled consumption (break-even), which caused settlements to grow even when they weren't actually gaining resources
- Now, population only grows when there's a genuine food surplus (foodProduced > foodConsumed)


